like a splash of cold water in the face  Aquaman has arrived and though it's  great it's also a little confusing  jammed with a century's worth of  undersea exposition don't worry though  we're here to help you keep track of all  those lost tribes and strange artifacts  so grab your life preserver because  here's a spoiler filled explanation of  the ending of Aquaman Arthur and Mary's  search for the legendary lost Trident of  King at land took them to some exotic  locales but none were more unexpected  than the center of the earth itself but  longtime comic book fans know that if  there's one place you should always  expect the unexpected it's the land of  Skartaris see in the 1970s DC Comics  series the warlord it was revealed that  scar Terrace is a prehistoric jungle  world accessible through portals that  connected to earth and after the  destruction of Atlantis a band of  refugees traveled through one of these  portals to Skartaris and founded new  atlantis though Aquaman didn't run into  any of the citizens of New Atlantis  during his brief time on the other side  of the portal it would make sense that  the final resting place of at land's  Trident was actually scar Terrace as it  would explain the fate of the missing  tribe which opens the door to a whole  new world of adventure quite literally  once Arthur finally got his hands on at  Lin's trident fans got to see an  incredibly confusing sequence where it  seemingly lit up the nervous systems of  a bunch of random sea creatures there  was no concrete explanation as to what  was actually happening  leaving viewers to wonder just what  exactly this mythical Trident actually  does other than spark up what appeared  to be a bonus level from Tetris effect  earlier in the film it said that the  Trident gave Atlin command of the Seas  the prevailing theory is that the  Trident essentially enhanced Aquaman's  natural ability to communicate with sea  life amplifying it to the point where he  could exert his will and actually  control it that would explain how he was  able to command the Curan as well as the  shark mounts used by king ORMs forces it  even seemed to extend to the trench  dwelling Atlantean descendants who had  devolved back into a more monstrous form  you have to hand it to princess Mara not  only did she save Atlantis and the  surface world as well she also managed  to free yourself from an unwanted  political marriage by replacing the  ambitious and scheming prince armed with  the much more suggestible and well kind  of dumber Arthur it was a brilliant  maneuver from the real power behind the  throne  mrs. ad your best thinking when you're  not thinking at all those worst pep talk  ever and Arthur is going to need Maris  political acumen because he's way out of  his depth no pun intended so far it  doesn't seem like he's even heard the  word diplomacy sure a lot was made of  Aquaman's unique ability to bring the  surface world and Atlantis together but  you have to be able to do more than talk  to fish to get that done you have to  talk to people and so far that doesn't  really seem to be his strong suit did  anybody really think Black Manta was  dead just because his head exploded and  he fell hundreds of feet into the angry  ocean bouncing off every single  outcropping of rock in Italy on the way  down of course not  considering the lengths to which  director James Wan went to and ordered  to shoehorn Manta and his original story  into a film that didn't need him there's  no way he was going to be written out  that easily so what can fans expect from  Manta in future Aquaman films well comic  book readers have a pretty good idea and  it ain't pretty way back in the 1970s  Black Manta was at the center of one of  the most shocking storylines in comics  history as he finally got his revenge on  Aquaman by murdering Arthur and Mary's  infant son we're not sure a sequel will  get quite that dark but Aquaman's dad is  still alive and would seem like a ripe  target for mantas vengeance especially  since the mid credit scene showed Manta  teamed up with Atlantis obsessed  researcher Stephen chin in the comics  Shin was a friend of Aquaman's dad who  betrayed them both to satisfy his  compulsion to find the location of  Atlantis so will things play out  similarly in the movies with black manta  and dr. shin working together not to  mention the continued danger of prince  or min the existence of star terrasse  one thing is for sure Aquaman 2 will  have no shortage of plot lines to choose  from besides giving him the ability to  command the creatures of the sea  the Trident of Atlin was also supposed  to serve as the ultimate trump card  granting Arthur the title of king of  Atlantis yet when he showed up with the  Trident to try and stop the Atlantean  Civil War surprisingly few people on  either side of the battle seemed to  actually notice or care at least at  first it's clear that his goal of  uniting the seven tribes of Atlantis is  going to take a whole lot more work than  just raising a lofty underwater  equivalent of xcalibur  as a wise man once said supreme  executive power derives from a mandate  from the masses not from some farcical  aquatic  ceremony becoming King isn't the end of  Arthur's work it's just the beginning  magic Trident or no magic trident  [Music]
 

